This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The session covered six sequential user requests, each building on the last:

   a. **"on peut enlever le remote github, puis merge"** — remove the `github` git remote (which contradicted the one-remote doctrine in CLAUDE.md) and merge PR #47 (the SBOM removal).

   b. **"est-ce qu'on peut configurer pour permettre la détection de race, il faut installer un compilateur c"** — enable the Go race detector locally, acknowledging a C compiler is needed.

   c. **"ajoute au backlog une nouvelle entrée : je souhaite retravailler le pull depuis la vue explorer, il faudra qu'on brainstorm sur la meilleure façon de le faire pour l'expérience utilisateur"** — record a backlog entry for reworking the explorer's pull, explicitly framed as needing a brainstorm on UX, so nothing pre-decided.

   d. **The brainstorm itself** — the user proposed a concrete design (new selection mode, multi-select parent folders, confirm → list of repos, per-row spinner then completion icon, target dir still indicated, explorer tree mirrored on disk as group directories, modals reserved for yes/no only) and asked me to analyse it. Across several turns they then settled: existing repos are skipped untouched; a future `sync` feature in the workspaces view handles dirty working copies; the workspaces-borrow mechanism for the target directory is kept; `gitlab.pull.target_dir` deleted; discovery and cloning pipelined; individual projects selectable; ticking a group takes everything under it with drill-in deselection; cancelling stops the pipeline but lets in-flight clones finish; the list is discarded on `esc`; `max_depth` deleted.

   e. **"fais la pagination"** — implement D34 (no pagination anywhere in `explorer/api.go`).

   f. **"renomme la branche et continue"** then **"enchaine directement"** — rename the branch and continue into the lighter discovery fetch, then into the rework itself.

   g. **"ok push"** and **"merge"** — push the groundwork as PR #49 and merge it.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Go, Bubble Tea (Elm architecture; **Rule 110**: only `Update()` mutates the model, `View()` read-only, `Cmd` does I/O and returns messages)
   - `errgroup` concurrency in the scan pipeline; nondeterministic completion ordering in tests
   - go-gitlab client (`gitlab.com/gitlab-org/api/client-go v1.10.0`): `ListOptions{Page, PerPage int64}`, `Response.NextPage int64` read from the `X-Next-Page` header
   - Go generics for a shared pagination helper
   - `httptest` fake GitLab servers routing by longest path prefix
   - `datatable.Model[T]` — generic table; `Column[T].Cell func(T) string` (plain text only, **Rule 122**); `Config.SelectedStyles func(T) table.Styles`; `Update` is a whitelist switch with **no `default`**, so unhandled keys (including `Space`) are never consumed; `SetItems` replaces items on every drill-down
   - `theme.CheckState` (`CheckNone`/`CheckAll`/`CheckSome`) and `theme.RenderCheckboxTri` — already shared primitives; `RenderCheckboxTri` applies styling so it **cannot** go inside a table cell
